I declare that I have used Gemini and GitHub Copilot as AI assistants to help me write, debug, and improve code for this
project submission. These tools were used to assist with code generation, error resolution, and general programming guidance.

I can confirm that I DID not use AI to generate the entire game from scratch.

Examples of prompts I have used:

- Help me find what the problem is with this code..
- Help me design level 1.
- How do i adjust the coordinates of the player, object and platforms.

-How do i make a player teleport and make some platforms move horizontally and vertically?

-How do i transform platforms into images?

Using AI helped me clarify technical requirements quickly and allowed me to focus more time on the
actual Java code structure and general knowledge of game design. I do admit that I have used it frequently
to help me with debugging and creating the game, but I have also put in a lot of my own work and creativity into the project.
Ultimately, the final product is a result of my own efforts and understanding of game development concepts.

